  <entry>
    <title>Affine</title>
    <id>https://pype.dev/affine/</id>
    <updated>2025-10-13T05:16:22Z</updated>
    <published>2025-10-13T05:16:22Z</published>
    <link href="https://pype.dev/affine/" rel="alternate" type="text/html"></link>
    <summary type="text">Mind-mapping webapp at home with native desktop App. Like Notion but with diagram support</summary>
    <content type="html">&lt;p&gt;Mind-mapping webapp at home with native desktop App. Like Notion but with diagram support&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;work&#34;&gt;&lt;span class=&#34;heading-wear-glyph&#34;&gt;Work&lt;/span&gt; &lt;a href=&#34;#work&#34; class=&#34;heading-anchor&#34;&gt;#&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The mind-mapping capabilities with Affine seem pretty great. There&amp;rsquo;s a few&#xA;quirks I&amp;rsquo;m trying to become aware of, like the edgeless and page modes show you&#xA;the same info, but there isn&amp;rsquo;t one view that makes &lt;em&gt;all&lt;/em&gt; the settings clear&amp;hellip;&#xA;so for example just adding another block on a page doesn&amp;rsquo;t make a new little&#xA;section in edgeless view - it just adds text to the existing blob. But in the&#xA;edgeless view I can click &lt;code&gt;+&lt;/code&gt; off the side of a box and get a new distinct&#xA;bubble that I can type in and such, but then back in teh pages view it just&#xA;looks like I added a block. so the block view on the page doesn&amp;rsquo;t represent the&#xA;other possible relationships whichi s fine, just need to be aware of it&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;ul&gt;&#xA;&lt;li&gt;I have another JFlo vid now&amp;hellip; falling behind&lt;/li&gt;&#xA;&lt;/ul&gt;&#xA;</content>
    <author>
      <name>Nic Payne</name>
      <uri>https://pype.dev</uri>
    </author>
  </entry>
